course: dictionary
lesson: 12072
title: A religious leader
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cleric is a religious leader. A priest, a minister, a rabbi and an imam are all clerics. Different faiths have different clerics, but each one leads people in their religion.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «The cleric read a prayer at the wedding.» A prayer is a religious message, and a wedding is a special ceremony, so a cleric must be a religious leader who leads the service. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The religious leader read a prayer at the wedding" still makes sense.
explain: Cleric is a more formal word than priest. News writers and history books use it for any religious leader, whatever their faith. In fantasy games, a cleric is a holy character who heals the others, so always check the clues to see which meaning fits.
fact: A cleric is a religious leader.
fact: Priests, ministers, rabbis and imams are all clerics.
fact: Cleric is a general word that covers leaders of any faith.
fact: Cleric is more formal than priest.
fact: In fantasy games, a cleric is a holy character who heals.
exercise: «The cleric read a prayer at the wedding.» What is a cleric? | A type of bird | *A religious leader, such as a priest or imam | A guest who sings at weddings | A person who cleans the church
exercise: «Many clerics of different faiths met to talk about peace.» What does faiths mean here? | Old stories about kings | *Religions | Schools | Football teams
exercise: Ruth says, «The news used cleric, so it must mean a priest only.» Why might a news writer choose cleric? | It is a casual word for a friend | *It is a formal word for any religious leader, whatever their faith | It means a priest in a church only | It means a doctor who works in a hospital
test: «In the fantasy game, my cleric healed my knight after the battle.» What is a cleric in this game? | A castle guard who sleeps all day | A sword-fighter who never heals | A horse that carries the packs | *A holy character who heals
test: Which of these is an example of a cleric? | A doctor | *A rabbi | A teacher | A postman
exam: Ruth says a cleric is a doctor, because clerics visit people in hospital. What is the right meaning of cleric? | *A religious leader, such as a priest or imam | A lawyer who works in court | A hospital helper who carries trays | A doctor who treats illness
